  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: Codec\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: Codec\n       Program: commons-codec\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Codec/Codec.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/commons-codec.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Codec/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 18\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: Codec-15\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\n28b7b958d39730fc278fd1919bf335c52133a1a2\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2015-03-22 18:48:52 +0000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\nCODEC-199\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CODEC-199\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.apache.commons.codec.language.SoundexTest::testHWRuleEx1\n   --> junit.framework.AssertionFailedError: expected:<Y3[3]0> but was:<Y3[0]0>\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.apache.commons.codec.language.Soundex\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: Bug in HW rule in Soundex\nType: Bug | Priority: Major | Status: Resolved | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nThe Soundex algorithm says that if two characters that map to the same code are separated by H or W, the second one is not encoded.\nHowever, in the implementation (in Soundex.getMappingCode() line 191), a character that is preceded by two characters that are either H or W, is not encoded, regardless of what the last consonant was.\nSource: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soundex#American_Soundex\n\nComments:\n\n[Gary D. Gregory]: Patches with unit tests are welcome :-)\n\n[Yossi Tamari]: Patch for the problematic method and adding a unit test attached.\n\n[Gary D. Gregory]: Fix is in trunk. Thank you. Please verify and close.\n\n[Yossi Tamari]: In the first patch I submitted I tried to localize the changes to reduce risk. Having thought about it since, I have a better patch which I think is more efficient (less map lookups), more correct (the HW rule is specific to the US English mapping, but it was implemented in the main code, I fixed this by defining a new mapping character of '#' that marks a silent letter, and mapping H and W to it), and I think results in simpler code.\nPatch attached as better.patch.\n\n[Gary D. Gregory]: Thank you Yossi. \n\nPatch applied and pushed to https://repository.apache.org/content/repositories/snapshots/commons-codec/commons-codec/1.11-SNAPSHOT/\n\nPlease verify and fix.\n\nGary",
  "fix_diff": "--- org.apache.commons.codec.language.Soundex (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.codec.language.Soundex (fixed)\n@@ -185,12 +185,13 @@\n         final char mappedChar = this.map(str.charAt(index));\n         // HW rule check\n         if (index > 1 && mappedChar != '0') {\n-            final char hwChar = str.charAt(index - 1);\n-            if ('H' == hwChar || 'W' == hwChar) {\n-                final char preHWChar = str.charAt(index - 2);\n-                final char firstCode = this.map(preHWChar);\n-                if (firstCode == mappedChar || 'H' == preHWChar || 'W' == preHWChar) {\n+            for (int i=index-1 ; i>=0 ; i--) {\n+                final char prevChar = str.charAt(i);\n+                if (this.map(prevChar)==mappedChar) {\n                     return 0;\n+                }\n+                if ('H'!=prevChar && 'W'!=prevChar) {\n+                    break;\n                 }\n             }\n         }"
}